      {
        "id": "read-model",
        "heading": "02 / Read the mechanism, not a result",
        "accent": "violet",
        "text": [
          "The two paths are a teaching comparison. The shared pre-fork copy and later token counts are authored symbols, not observations from an experiment."
        ],
        "bullets": [
          "Incoming +RNA is a pill in the cell and a solid strand in the close-up. The dashed complementary strand is an intermediate; separate tray tokens stand for completed new +RNA.",
          "The cytoplasmic drawing simplifies a membrane-associated replication process and omits sequence, molecular structure, cofactors, host responses, and time.",
          "The alternate path assumes the pre-fork copy can join existing proteins and leave the cell. Assembly coupling varies among viruses; the outside particles are not measured yield or intervention efficacy.",
          "Checkpoint: explain why protein production can continue without guaranteeing a supply of new complete genomes."
        ]
      },
